(Thus we need a different way to get confirmed true without affecting locked status. There's unload_origin_payload which sets confirmed true but does not affect locked. However unload requires origin_payload_linked true and origin_node_occupied true, and not origin_availability_confirmed. It also sets origin_node_ready true (already maybe), cargo_available true, and removes payload link. So we could: load origin payload (locked true, occupied true, payload linked, cargo false), then unload origin payload (confirmed true, cargo true, payload link false, locked remains true). This yields locked true, confirmed true, occupied true, ready? We still need origin_node_ready true; we can activate node before load (makes ready true). Load does not affect ready. Unload does not affect ready. So after unload we have origin_node_ready true, origin_node_occupied true, origin_availability_locked true, origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true, origin_payload_linked false. This matches goal for origin (except we also need cargo_available? not required). Good.)
(Thus we can achieve origin confirmed and locked via load then unload.)
(Similarly for destination.)
(Now we need transport leg assembled after we have origin and destination confirmed? Actually assemble_transport_leg requires origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed (both true) and origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, transport_leg_available. It does not require locked. So we can assemble after we have confirmed both (which we get after unload). Good.)
(Thus plan steps:)
(For each availability (origin and destination):)
(1. Activate node (make ready))
(2. Allocate vehicle unit (if needed))
(3. Attach task profile)
(4. Confirm candidate preparedness (makes candidate_prepared))
(5. Assign operator resource (for locking))
(6. Load payload (locks, occupies, cargo false, payload linked))
(7. Unload payload (confirms, cargo true, payload link false, keeps locked and occupied))
(After both availabilities processed, we have:)
(- origin_node_ready true (from activation))
(- origin_node_occupied true (from load))
(- origin_availability_locked true (from load))
(- origin_availability_confirmed true (from unload))
(- cargo_available true (after unload))
(- Similarly for destination.)
(Now we need to assemble transport leg: use assemble_transport_leg (requires origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, transport_leg_available). After that we get transport_leg_assembled, origin_linked, destination_linked, not transport_leg_available.)
(Then we need transport_leg_loading_authorized true. Use authorize_transport_leg_loading: requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized. We have origin_availability_locked true (from load). Need candidate_task_profile_linked for origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha. We attached task profile earlier, so yes. So we can authorize.)
(Now we need dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha: currently it's allocated to shift_candidate_alpha (candidate_dispatch_slot_linked). We need to free it. We can execute execute_schedule_dispatch for shift_candidate_alpha (which will set dispatched true, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma, dispatch_slot_available true). This also requires dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha (true), candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha ?vehicle_unit (we have vehicle_unit_gamma), candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha (true), and not dispatched shift_candidate_alpha (currently false). So we can execute that.)
(Now we also need vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha true (goal). We allocated vehicle to destination earlier.)
(We also need vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma true (goal). After dispatch, vehicle_unit_gamma becomes available.)
(We also need compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha true. Currently it's linked to shift_candidate_alpha. We need to release it. Use release_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha. This will make it available and unlink.)
(Now we need to check that any other goal conditions are satisfied: candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha and origin_availability_alpha (we did confirm_candidate_preparedness). candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (we attached). candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta (we allocated vehicle_unit_beta to destination and attached vehicle link via allocate_vehicle_unit which also sets candidate_vehicle_linked). dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha (after dispatch). dispatched shift_candidate_alpha (after dispatch). origin_availability_confirmed true (after unload). origin_availability_locked true (after load). origin_node_occupied true (after load). origin_node_ready true (after activation). destination similarly. transport_leg_assembled true (after assemble). transport_leg_destination_linked true (after assemble). transport_leg_loading_authorized true (after authorize). transport_leg_origin_linked true (after assemble). vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha true (after allocate). vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma true (after dispatch). compliance_certificate_available true (after release). Also need to ensure that we didn't accidentally make any false predicates that goal expects true but we might have made false via other actions.)
(Check each action's effects to ensure we don't inadvertently delete needed predicates.)
(Let's list actions and their effects:)
(- activate_origin_node: effect (origin_node_ready ?origin_node). No negative effects. Good.)
(- allocate_vehicle_unit ?candidate ?vehicle_unit: effect (vehicle_allocated ?candidate), (candidate_vehicle_linked ?candidate ?vehicle_unit), (not (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit)). So it consumes vehicle availability.)
(- attach_task_profile ?candidate ?route_task_profile: effect (candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile), (not (route_task_profile_available ?route_task_profile)). So consumes route task profile availability.)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness ?candidate ?route_task_profile: effect (candidate_prepared ?candidate). No negative.)
(- assign_operator_resource ?candidate ?operator_resource: effect (candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource), (not (operator_available ?operator_resource)). Consumes operator availability.)
(- load_origin_payload ?origin_availability ?origin_node ?route_task_profile ?payload_unit: effect (origin_node_occupied ?origin_node), (origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability), (origin_payload_linked ?origin_availability ?payload_unit), (not (cargo_available ?payload_unit)). No effect on origin_node_ready or origin_availability_confirmed.)
(- unload_origin_payload ?origin_availability ?origin_node ?route_task_profile ?payload_unit: effect (origin_node_ready ?origin_node), (origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability), (cargo_available ?payload_unit), (not (origin_payload_linked ?origin_availability ?payload_unit)). No effect on origin_availability_locked or origin_node_occupied.)
(- activate_destination_node similar.)
(- load_destination_payload similar effects: destination_node_occupied, destination_availability_locked, destination_payload_linked, not cargo_available.)
(- unload_destination_payload: effect destination_node_ready, destination_availability_confirmed, cargo_available, not destination_payload_linked.)
(- assemble_transport_leg: effect (transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg), (transport_leg_origin_linked ?transport_leg ?origin_node), (transport_leg_destination_linked ?transport_leg ?destination_node), (not (transport_leg_available ?transport_leg)). No negative on others.)
(- authorize_transport_leg_loading: effect (transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg). No negative.)
(- execute_schedule_dispatch ?candidate ?vehicle_unit ?dispatch_slot: effect (dispatched ?candidate), (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit), (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot). No negative on other predicates (except maybe candidate_dispatch_slot_linked? Not removed). It does not remove candidate_dispatch_slot_linked; that remains true. That's fine.)
(- release_compliance_certificate ?candidate ?compliance_certificate: effect (compliance_certificate_available ?compliance_certificate), (not (candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_candidate)). So it removes the link.)
(Now we need to ensure we don't inadvertently cause any goal predicate to become false due to negative effects.)
(Goal predicates we need to stay true at end:)
(- candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha: we set true via confirm_candidate_preparedness; no action removes candidate_prepared (no negative). Good.)
(- candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha: same.)
(- candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha: we set via attach_task_profile; no action removes it (detach_task_profile could, but we won't use). So stays.)
(- candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta: set via allocate_vehicle_unit; no action removes (detach? none). Good.)
(- compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha: set via release_compliance_certificate; no action removes it (assign_compliance_certificate would remove availability, but we won't assign again). Good.)
(- destination_availability_confirmed destination_availability_alpha: set via unload_destination_payload; no action removes it (lock_destination_availability would set confirmed true as well, but not remove). Actually lock_destination_availability also sets confirmed true (adds). There's no action that removes confirmed. So stays.)
(- destination_availability_locked destination_availability_alpha: set via load_destination_payload; no action removes it (unload does not affect locked). Good.)
(- destination_node_occupied destination_node_alpha: set via load_destination_payload; no action removes it (unload does not affect occupied). Good.)
(- destination_node_ready destination_node_alpha: set via activate_destination_node; no action removes it (load/unload do not affect ready). Good.)
(- dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha: set via execute_schedule_dispatch; no action removes it (allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate would remove availability, but we won't). Good.)
(- dispatched shift_candidate_alpha: set via execute_schedule_dispatch; no action removes it. Good.)
(- origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha: set via unload_origin_payload; same reasoning.)
(- origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha: set via load_origin_payload; unload does not affect locked. Good.)
(- origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha: set via load_origin_payload; unload does not affect occupied. Good.)
(- origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha: set via activate_origin_node; load/unload do not affect ready. Good.)
(- transport_leg_assembled transport_leg_alpha: set via assemble_transport_leg; no action removes it (disassemble? none). Good.)
(- transport_leg_destination_linked transport_leg_alpha destination_node_alpha: set via assemble_transport_leg; no removal.)
(- transport_leg_loading_authorized transport_leg_alpha: set via authorize_transport_leg_loading; no removal.)
(- transport_leg_origin_linked transport_leg_alpha origin_node_alpha: set via assemble_transport_leg; no removal.)
(- vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha: set via allocate_vehicle_unit; no removal.)
(- vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma: set via execute_schedule_dispatch; no removal (allocate_vehicle_unit would remove availability, but we won't allocate gamma to anything else). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure we don't accidentally make any of these false via other actions we might include inadvertently. We'll stick to the minimal set.)
(Now we need to consider any preconditions that may not be satisfied at the time we attempt actions.)
(Let's design step-by-step.)
(Initial state:)
(- candidate_created origin_availability_alpha true.)
(- vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha true.)
(- candidate_vehicle_linked origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_alpha true.)
(- cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha true.)
(- origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha true.)
(- origin_node_ready? false initially.)
(- origin_node_occupied? false.)
(Similarly for destination:)
(- candidate_created destination_availability_alpha true.)
(- vehicle_allocated? false initially.)
(- candidate_vehicle_linked? false.)
(- cargo_available true.)
(- destination_availability_node_linked destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha true.)
(- destination_node_ready? false.)
(- destination_node_occupied? false.)
(- operator_available driver_operator_alpha true.)
(We also have shift_candidate_alpha etc but not needed for origin/destination preparation except maybe we need operator for lock? Actually lock does not need operator; load/unload does not need operator. So we may not need to assign operator at all! Wait load_origin_payload does not require operator. So we can skip assign_operator_resource. However lock_origin_availability is not needed; we are using load/unload to get locked and confirmed. So we don't need operator for origin/destination. Good.)
(Thus we can skip assign_operator_resource.)
(Now we need to attach task profile to origin and destination. For that we need route_task_profile_available route_task_profile_alpha (true initially). After attaching to origin, it becomes unavailable; then we need another copy for destination? We only have one route_task_profile_alpha object. The predicate route_task_profile_available is per object; after we attach to origin, it becomes unavailable (not available). To attach to destination we would need another route_task_profile instance, but we only have one. However goal only requires candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha. It does not require destination to have task profile linked. So we only need to attach task profile to origin, not destination. Good.)
(Thus we attach task profile to origin_availability_alpha only.)
(Now we need to allocate vehicle to origin and destination. Origin already has vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_alpha (from init). So we don't need to allocate vehicle for origin; it's already allocated and linked to vehicle_unit_alpha. However goal requires candidate_vehicle_linked origin_availability_alpha? Not required. Goal does not require origin vehicle link. So we can leave as is.)
(Destination needs vehicle_allocated and candidate_vehicle_linked to vehicle_unit_beta. We'll allocate vehicle_unit_beta to destination_availability_alpha.)
(Now we need to confirm candidate_prepared for origin and destination. For origin, we need candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha. Precondition: candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, candidate_task_profile_linked, not candidate_prepared. We have candidate_created true, vehicle_allocated true (already), we need to attach task profile (we will), then confirm_preparedness.)
(For destination: need candidate_created true, vehicle_allocated (we will allocate), candidate_task_profile_linked? Not required for goal but confirm_candidate_preparedness requires candidate_task_profile_linked. So we need to attach task profile to destination as well to be able to confirm preparedness. However goal does not require destination task profile linked. But we need it for preparing. We could attach task profile to destination, but we only have one route_task_profile_alpha. However after we attach to origin, it becomes unavailable. We could attach to destination first, then later we need origin task profile linked for goal. But we need both origin and destination to have task profile linked for preparing them. Since we only have one route_task_profile, we cannot have both linked simultaneously. However maybe we can prepare origin without task profile? Let's check confirm_candidate_preparedness precondition: requires candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile. So yes, requires link.)
(Thus we need to have task profile linked to each candidate when we prepare them. But we can prepare one, then detach task profile (making it available again) and attach to the other. However detach_task_profile will remove the link, making candidate_not_prepared? Actually candidate_prepared remains true (no effect). Detach only removes the link and makes route_task_profile_available. So we can prepare origin, then detach task profile from origin (but candidate_prepared stays true), making task profile available again, then attach to destination, prepare destination, then optionally re-attach to origin if needed for goal (goal requires origin task profile linked). So we need to end with origin task profile linked. So we can: attach to origin, prepare origin, detach, attach to destination, prepare destination, detach, attach to origin again (to satisfy goal). However we need to ensure that after detaching, origin remains prepared (candidate_prepared stays true). That's fine.)
(Alternatively we could prepare origin first using task profile, then after preparing we detach, prepare destination using same task profile, then re-attach to origin for goal. That's fine.)
(Now we also need to consider that load/unload payload actions require candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile? Actually load_origin_payload precondition: (candidate_prepared ?origin_availability) (candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile) (origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node) (destination? wait load_origin_payload only uses origin_availability, origin_node, route_task_profile, payload). Yes load_origin_payload requires candidate_task_profile_linked. Similarly unload_origin_payload also requires candidate_task_profile_linked. So we need task profile linked during load and unload as well.)
(Thus we need task profile linked for origin during load/unload steps. Similarly for destination load/unload requires task profile linked for destination.)
(Thus we need to have task profile linked to each availability at the time of load/unload. Since we only have one, we need to sequence: attach to origin, prepare origin, load origin payload, unload origin payload, detach task profile from origin (makes it available), attach to destination, prepare destination, load destination payload, unload destination payload, detach task profile from destination, then attach to origin again for goal (since goal requires origin task profile linked). After that we may not need to load/unload again (since we already have origin locked/confirmed etc). But attaching after unload does not affect those states. So final attach to origin will set candidate_task_profile_linked true again (good) and make route_task_profile unavailable (but we don't need it after). That's fine.)
(Now we need to ensure that after we detach from origin, origin remains prepared, locked, confirmed, occupied, ready, etc. Detach only affects task profile link and route_task_profile availability. So fine.)
(Now we need to also consider that load_origin_payload requires origin_availability_node_linked (true), cargo_available (true initially), not origin_availability_locked (false initially). After we activate node, origin_node_ready true, origin_node_occupied false. So load will work.)
(After load, origin_availability_locked true, cargo false, origin_payload_linked true, origin_node_occupied true.)
(Unload requires origin_availability_locked true, origin_payload_linked true, origin_node_occupied true, not origin_availability_confirmed (false initially). After unload, we get origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true, origin_payload_linked false, origin_node_ready true (effect), origin_node_occupied stays true, origin_availability_locked stays true.)
(Thus after unload we have all desired.)
(Now we need to do similar for destination.)
(Now we need to allocate vehicle to destination: allocate_vehicle_unit destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta. Precondition: candidate_created destination_availability_alpha true, not vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha true, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta true (init). After allocation, vehicle_allocated destination true, candidate_vehicle_linked destination vehicle_unit_beta true, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta becomes false.)
(Now we need to prepare destination: need candidate_task_profile_linked destination route_task_profile_alpha (we will attach after detaching from origin). So we need to have task profile available.)
(Now we also need to activate destination node before load: activate_destination_node requires candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha, candidate_task_profile_linked destination route_task_profile_alpha, destination_availability_node_linked, not destination_node_ready, not destination_node_occupied. So we need to have candidate_prepared and task profile linked before activation. So order: attach task profile to destination, confirm preparedness, activate node, load payload, unload payload, detach task profile.)
(Now we need to ensure we have operator? Not needed for load/unload.)
(Now we need to ensure we have transport leg assembled after both availabilities are confirmed (after unloads). assemble_transport_leg requires origin_availability_confirmed true, destination_availability_confirmed true, origin_node_ready true, destination_node_ready true, transport_leg_available true. After we finish origin and destination processing, we will have those true. transport_leg_available is true initially (not used yet). So we can assemble.)
(Now we need to authorize transport leg loading: requires transport_leg_assembled true, origin_availability_locked true, candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha, not transport_leg_loading_authorized. After we re-attach task profile to origin (for goal), we will have candidate_task_profile_linked origin route_task_profile_alpha true. origin_availability_locked true (from load). So we can authorize.)
(Now we need to execute dispatch for shift_candidate_alpha: requires dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha true (init), candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha ?vehicle_unit (we have vehicle_unit_gamma), candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha true, not dispatched shift_candidate_alpha false. So we can dispatch.)
(Now we need to release compliance certificate: release_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha. Precondition: candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha (true). Effect: compliance_certificate_available true, unlink.)
(Now we need to ensure we haven't used up any resources needed later: e.g., we used vehicle_unit_beta for destination allocation; after that vehicle_unit_beta becomes unavailable (not available). Goal does not require vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta; it's okay if it's false. Goal only requires vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma (true) and vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (true). So fine.)
(We also used loading containers? Not needed for goal; we didn't use loading_container actions. So we can skip them.)
(We also need to ensure we didn't inadvertently use loading_container_linked etc that might affect something else but not needed.)
(Now we need to verify that we haven't violated any negative preconditions (like not (something) that becomes true). We'll check each action's preconditions.)
(Let's outline detailed steps with objects.)
(We'll use shorthand names:)
(- OA = origin_availability_alpha)
(- DA = destination_availability_alpha)
(- SCa = shift_candidate_alpha)
(- VG = vehicle_unit_gamma)
(- VB = vehicle_unit_beta)
(- VA = vehicle_unit_alpha (already linked to OA))
(- RTP = route_task_profile_alpha)
(- TL = transport_leg_alpha)
(- ON = origin_node_alpha)
(- DN = destination_node_alpha)
(- DSS = dispatch_slot_alpha)
(- CC = compliance_certificate_alpha)
(- Op = driver_operator_alpha (maybe not needed))
(- Cargo = cargo_payload_alpha)
(We'll also need loading container? Not needed.)
(Now steps:)
(1. Attach task profile to OA: attach_task_profile OA RTP)
(Precondition: candidate_created OA (true), vehicle_allocated OA (true), route_task_profile_available RTP (true).)
(Effect: candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP true, route_task_profile_available RTP becomes false.)
(2. Confirm preparedness OA: confirm_candidate_preparedness OA RTP)
(Precondition: candidate_created OA (true), vehicle_allocated OA (true), candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP (now true), not candidate_prepared OA (false initially).)
(Effect: candidate_prepared OA true.)
(3. Activate origin node: activate_origin_node OA ON RTP)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared OA (true), candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP (true), origin_availability_node_linked OA ON (true), not origin_node_ready ON (true), not origin_node_occupied ON (true).)
(Effect: origin_node_ready ON true.)
(4. Load origin payload: load_origin_payload OA ON RTP Cargo)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared OA (true), candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP (true), origin_availability_node_linked OA ON (true), cargo_available Cargo (true), not origin_availability_locked OA (false currently).)
(Effect: origin_node_occupied ON true, origin_availability_locked OA true, origin_payload_linked OA Cargo true, not cargo_available Cargo.)
(5. Unload origin payload: unload_origin_payload OA ON RTP Cargo)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared OA (true), candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP (true), origin_availability_node_linked OA ON (true), origin_node_occupied ON (true), origin_payload_linked OA Cargo true, not origin_availability_confirmed OA (false currently).)
(Effect: origin_node_ready ON true (already true), origin_availability_confirmed OA true, cargo_available Cargo true, not origin_payload_linked OA Cargo.)
(Now after these steps, OA has: candidate_prepared true, candidate_task_profile_linked true, origin_node_ready true, origin_node_occupied true, origin_availability_locked true, origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true, origin_payload_linked false.)
(Now we need to detach task profile from OA to free it for DA.)
(6. Detach task profile from OA: detach_task_profile OA RTP)
(Precondition: candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP (true).)
(Effect: route_task_profile_available RTP true, not candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP.)
(Now OA loses task profile link, but candidate_prepared remains true.)
(Now prepare destination.)
(7. Allocate vehicle to DA: allocate_vehicle_unit DA VB)
(Precondition: candidate_created DA (true), not vehicle_allocated DA (true), vehicle_available VB (true).)
(Effect: vehicle_allocated DA true, candidate_vehicle_linked DA VB true, vehicle_available VB false.)
(8. Attach task profile to DA: attach_task_profile DA RTP)
(Precondition: candidate_created DA (true), vehicle_allocated DA (true), route_task_profile_available RTP (true) (now true after detach).)
(Effect: candidate_task_profile_linked DA RTP true, route_task_profile_available RTP false.)
(9. Confirm preparedness DA: confirm_candidate_preparedness DA RTP)
(Precondition: candidate_created DA (true), vehicle_allocated DA (true), candidate_task_profile_linked DA RTP (true), not candidate_prepared DA (false).)
(Effect: candidate_prepared DA true.)
(10. Activate destination node: activate_destination_node DA DN RTP)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared DA (true), candidate_task_profile_linked DA RTP (true), destination_availability_node_linked DA DN (true), not destination_node_ready DN (true), not destination_node_occupied DN (true).)
(Effect: destination_node_ready DN true.)
(11. Load destination payload: load_destination_payload DA DN Cargo)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared DA (true), candidate_task_profile_linked DA RTP (true), destination_availability_node_linked DA DN (true), cargo_available Cargo (true after origin unload), not destination_availability_locked DA (false).)
(Effect: destination_node_occupied DN true, destination_availability_locked DA true, destination_payload_linked DA Cargo true, not cargo_available Cargo.)
(12. Unload destination payload: unload_destination_payload DA DN Cargo)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared DA (true), candidate_task_profile_linked DA RTP (true), destination_availability_node_linked DA DN (true), destination_node_occupied DN true, destination_payload_linked DA Cargo true, not destination_availability_confirmed DA (false).)
(Effect: destination_node_ready DN true, destination_availability_confirmed DA true, cargo_available Cargo true, not destination_payload_linked DA Cargo.)
(Now after these, DA has: candidate_prepared true, candidate_task_profile_linked true, destination_node_ready true, destination_node_occupied true, destination_availability_locked true, destination_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true, destination_payload_linked false.)
(Now we have task profile linked to DA; we need to detach it to free for OA re-attach.)
(13. Detach task profile from DA: detach_task_profile DA RTP)
(Precondition: candidate_task_profile_linked DA RTP (true).)
(Effect: route_task_profile_available RTP true, not candidate_task_profile_linked DA RTP.)
(Now DA loses task profile link but remains prepared etc.)
(Now we need to attach task profile to OA again for goal.)
(14. Attach task profile to OA: attach_task_profile OA RTP)
(Precondition: candidate_created OA (true), vehicle_allocated OA (true), route_task_profile_available RTP (true) (now true after detach).)
(Effect: candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP true, route_task_profile_available RTP false.)
(Now OA has task profile linked again (good for goal). OA remains prepared etc.)
(Now we need to assemble transport leg.)
(15. Assemble transport leg: assemble_transport_leg OA DA ON DN TL)
(Precondition: origin_availability_locked OA? Wait assemble_transport_leg precondition: origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability, destination_availability_locked ?destination_availability, origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node, destination_availability_node_linked ?destination_availability ?destination_node, origin_node_ready ?origin_node, destination_node_ready ?destination_node, origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability, destination_availability_confirmed ?destination_availability, transport_leg_available ?transport_leg.)
(Let's check: we have origin_availability_locked OA true (from load, still true). destination_availability_locked DA true (from load). origin_availability_node_linked OA ON true. destination_availability_node_linked DA DN true. origin_node_ready ON true (from activation). destination_node_ready DN true (from activation). origin_availability_confirmed OA true (from unload). destination_availability_confirmed DA true (from unload). transport_leg_available TL true (init). So all satisfied.)
(Effect: transport_leg_assembled TL true, transport_leg_origin_linked TL ON true, transport_leg_destination_linked TL DN true, not transport_leg_available TL.)
(Now we need to authorize transport leg loading.)
(16. Authorize transport leg loading: authorize_transport_leg_loading TL OA RTP)
(Precondition: transport_leg_assembled TL true, origin_availability_locked OA true, candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP (true after re-attach), not transport_leg_loading_authorized TL (false).)
(Effect: transport_leg_loading_authorized TL true.)
(Now we need to dispatch shift_candidate_alpha.)
